body:
`buildReverseColumnMap()` silently overwrites entries when two fields resolve to the same physical `columnName` (e.g., two fields both map to `createdAt`). That can cause incorrect protocol↔storage translation with no signal. Consider detecting duplicate resolved column names and throwing (or returning a multi-map) so collisions are surfaced early; adding a unit test for the collision case would lock this behavior in.
```suggestion
   * @throws Error if multiple fields resolve to the same physical column name.
  buildReverseColumnMap(fields: Record<string, { columnName?: string }>): Record<string, string> {
    const map: Record<string, string> = {};
    for (const key of Object.keys(fields)) {
      const col = fields[key].columnName ?? key;
      if (Object.prototype.hasOwnProperty.call(map, col) && map[col] !== key) {
        throw new Error(
          `StorageNameMapping.buildReverseColumnMap: duplicate columnName '${col}' for field keys '${map[col]}' and '${key}'`
        );
      }
```
